Validation round 08 fixes (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): frame-generation quality keys live without arming unused
swapchains, and keys off as fast as 0.7.0.
- apply_embedded_control no longer arms swapchains still flagged generation_eligible_pending. Each control revision
  armed DCS's early swapchains (enumerated, never named by a projection layer): four synthesizers that never composed a
  frame, the first live change stalling the frame thread 1.62 s and each later one about 0.63 s. A swapchain a
  projection layer uses is armed by the frame path, as at the start. A quality-key-only change, generation on before
  and after, keeps an arming thread's work (its take-in sets the keys without a rebuild). Tested: live-ini with an
  unused swapchain (fake runtime, D3D12 / D3D11 / flight) makes no private swapchain and logs no ready record or
  history for it.
- Flight log: live_settings result=5, one record per synthesizer each time its settings are set (made, quality keys
  set live, rebuilt): quality keys, why, the composition's quality bits; b= the swapchain.
- OFXR_LiveFgContract ("DCSC-OFXR-LIVE-FG/2"), exported, so DCS Control can tell this live contract (the quality keys
  set live with no swapchain armed by the change) from 0104's by the DLL's bytes.
- Keys off costs what 0.7.0 cost (validation round 08: comp+pack per pair in the 30-fps regime 214 -> 385 us with every
  new key off). The quality options' code, never taken with the keys off, made every NVIDIA composition about twice
  the instructions and 3X's composition slower on hardware (fg_triple_bench, 5424 x 5356 x 2, RTX: 0103 2073 us).
  frame_synthesis.hlsl now compiles them only with XRFG_FG_EXTRAS=1: every existing composition is the same bytecode
  as 0103's (checked with fxc), and an _extras twin of each of the 40 NVIDIA compositions (plain, masked, depth, MV,
  depth+MV) carries them. The synthesizer registers a twin for each composition it makes, binds it only for a pair
  with a quality bit (pair_extras), and makes its pipeline on first use (at creation when the options already have a
  key on). Measured, keys off: 3X 2075 us, 2X 1229 us (0103: 2074 / 1229-1238); all quality keys on, 3X 2746 us, 2X
  1349 us. The DLL grows by about 4.8 MB.
- tests/fg_triple_bench.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_TRIPLE_BENCH, label bench): the composition with DCS's mask and MVs in 2X and
  3X, keys from XRFG_TEST_FG_TRIPLE_QUALITY; written so it builds against 0001-0103 too.
(The 0.7.1 development series also had an occlusion fill around moving aircraft, [ofxr] dcs_motion_occlusion_fill, and
its engine-data fixtures; both were removed before release: in flight the fill never fired in the cockpit view, and in
the external view it made the halo around an aircraft worse by day.)

